---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../consts';

// Exempt from the site's ASD-STE100 rules. See scripts/ste-check.mjs.
// This page supplements Apple's standard EULA. It is not a custom App Store EULA.
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Rules for using the Suwatte app and website."
  meta={`Version ${LEGAL.termsVersion} · Effective ${LEGAL.termsEffective}`}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In short.</strong> Suwatte is a reader. It does not come with content or a catalogue.
      You choose the files, Servers, and third-party Sources that it uses, and you must use them
      lawfully.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. The app licence</h2>

  <p>
    If you download Suwatte from Apple's App Store, your licence to use the app is governed by the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">
      Apple Standard End User License Agreement
    </a>. We do not replace it with a custom App Store licence.
  </p>

  <p>
    These terms set rules for using the app and this website. They supplement the Apple Standard
    EULA. If these terms conflict with that EULA about your licence to the app, the EULA controls.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Suwatte does</h2>

  <p>
    Suwatte reads content that you add in one of three ways: physical files that you select,
    Servers that you connect, and Sources that you install. Suwatte ships with no Sources, content,
    or catalogue. We do not operate a content service, and content requests do not pass through a
    Suwatte server.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Lawful use</h2>

  <p>You must not use Suwatte or this website to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>infringe copyright, trade mark, privacy, or another person's rights;</li>
    <li>access or distribute material that you are not lawfully entitled to use;</li>
    <li>break a law or the terms of a service that you choose to access;</li>
    <li>circumvent access controls or interfere with a service; or</li>
    <li>create or distribute a Source for one of those purposes.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    You are responsible for the content and services that you choose and for protecting the
    credentials that you enter.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-party Sources, Servers, and websites</h2>

  <p>
    A Source is a third-party plugin that runs on your device with network access. A Server is a
    Komga, Kavita, or OPDS service that you operate or are authorised to use. We do not write, review,
    approve, endorse, or control third-party Sources, Source lists, Servers, or the websites that
    they access.
  </p>

  <p>
    Those services can change or stop working without notice. Their own terms and privacy policies
    apply. Install Sources only from lists that you trust, and connect only to Servers that you are
    authorised to use.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>

  <p>
    The Suwatte app, website, name, marks, and original design are protected by intellectual
    property law. These terms do not give you ownership of them or of third-party content.
  </p>

  <p>
    We do not host content reached through a third-party Source or Server. Send a notice about that
    content to the operator that hosts it. If you believe the app itself or material that we publish
    on this website infringes your rights, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> with your contact details, a
    description of the work, the location of the material, and the reason that you believe the use
    is unauthorised.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your data and backups</h2>

  <p>
    You are responsible for keeping copies of data that matters to you. iCloud sync, Suwatte JSON
    backups, and downloaded files are different systems and do not contain the same information.
    Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and the{' '}
    <a href="/docs/backups/">backup guide</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Availability and changes</h2>

  <p>
    We may add, change, suspend, or remove features and publish updates. We cannot guarantee that a
    third-party Source, Server, website, or file format will remain available or compatible.
  </p>

  <p>
    We may update these terms. The version and effective date at the top identify the current
    terms. We will call out material changes where practical.
  </p>

  <h2>8. This website</h2>

  <p>
    The website and its documentation are provided for general information. We try to keep them
    accurate, but they may contain errors or lag behind the current app. To the extent permitted by
    law, the website is provided as is. Nothing here limits a consumer right that cannot lawfully be
    limited.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Send questions about these terms to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .callout {
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
  }

  .callout p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }
</style>
